<div class="flex_column av-2nn3s7-76b4418b066adfc6db3156365cd01be3 av_one_full avia-builder-el-47 avia-builder-el-no-sibling first flex_column_div"><div class="av-special-heading av-m8oqolzi-1cd86dc86d7b3fd139f35a6eae4fe751 av-special-heading-h4 custom-color-heading blockquote modern-quote modern-centered avia-builder-el-48 el_before_av_textblock avia-builder-el-first av-inherit-size"><h4 class="av-special-heading-tag" itemprop="headline">Hematology and Biochemistry Testing</h4><div class="special-heading-border"><div class="special-heading-inner-border"></div></div></div>
<section class="av_textblock_section av-m8oqp26f-ac80ffae3765852f7b5f739daf01a5b1" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/CreativeWork"><div class="avia_textblock" itemprop="text"><p>Hematology and biochemistry play vital roles in assessing your health. Together, these tests contribute significantly to early diagnosis, enabling timely addiction treatments and better health outcomes.</p>
<p>A full-hematological analysis examines red and white blood cells, hemoglobin, and platelets to provide insights into overall health. A Full Chemical Analysis evaluates essential biochemical markers, offering a broad view of metabolic health, liver and kidney function, and electrolyte balance. Immune Response Analysis is crucial for understanding how well the immune system functions and the body’s response to infections and inflammation.</p>
<p>Regular monitoring through these analyses can help you maintain optimal health and well-being, provide peace of mind, and inform you of necessary lifestyle adjustments or interventions.</p>
</div></section></div>
